hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15550","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abu Uways narrated to us: Shurahbil narrated to us, from Jabbar ibn Sakhr al-Ansari, one of Banu Salamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, while on the road of Makkah: Who will outpace us to al-Uthayah? Abu Uways said: It is where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us forth, that he dam its basin and precede therein and fill it until we come to him. He said: Jabbar said: So I stood and said: I. He said: Go. So I went and came to al-Uthayah, and dammed its basin and preceded therein and filled it. Then my eyes overcame me and I slept. I woke only by a man whose mount was pulling him to the water while he was holding it back from it, and he said: O owner of the basin. And it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Yes. He said: So he brought his mount, then turned away and made it kneel, then said: Follow me with the edawah. So I followed him with it, and he performed wudu and perfected his wudu, and I performed wudu with him. Then he stood praying, and I stood at his left, and he took my hand and moved me to his right. So we prayed. It was only a little before the people came."
